WEBVTT

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:32.220
Today, it's miso soup with potatoes and seaweed!

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:34.670
Huh?

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.640
A lot has happened, grandma.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.720
Today is my first day working at the newspaper company.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:48.000
I'll have to do my best!

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:55.510
I think I'll make miso soup with potatoes and seaweed.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:32.890
My First Paper Delivery

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.220
Good morning!

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.240
Huh?

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:50.480
It can't be...

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.870
Flying Saucer Monster Ganagana

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.950
Everyone got abducted by aliens

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.600
and now they're being used in all sorts of sordid human experiments!

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.010
Grandma, help!

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.090
Like that would even happen.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:24.350
Ah, thank goodness.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:29.380
Everyone will be back soon, right?

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:30.520
Yeah.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:32.370
What is it?

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:35.120
Uhh... I was just wondering if there

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:37.520
was anyone who doesn't like potatoes in their miso soup?

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:39.020
I doubt it.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:40.380
Oh really?

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:46.030
Is there someone who prefers bread?

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:47.280
I'm sure it's fine.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.870
Either way.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.020
Okay.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:55.360
I was thinking... maybe it would be better if I made a lot, so that...

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:58.230
What is WRONG with you?

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:01.350
I was thinking about how terrible it would be,
if you were kidnapped

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:02.670
by aliens...

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:06.260
Don't tell me you're still thinking about that?

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.630
Well, it's more that the aliens would...

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:10.550
Aliens don't exist!

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.820
You're right.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:15.480
Don't worry.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.960
I'm not going anywhere.

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:20.300
Okay!

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:26.650
Hey?

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:28.450
Yes?

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:32.860
When you're done with the cooking, want to go out for a bit?

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:37.810
Out with the chief.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.330
Be back soon.

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:40.430
Kana.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.760
Can you take these?

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.600
What are they?

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:49.380
It's the paper route with the recipients' addresses.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:52.200
The first step is looking at that list and memorizing it.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:54.080
Wow...!

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:59.280
Even foreigners read the Fuushin Gazette!

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.330
Foreigners?

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:03.740
It says "Tom" here.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:06.730
That's just an abbreviation for "across from the neighbors".

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:07.690
[TOnari = neighbors, MUkai = across, TOMU = Tom]

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:11.030
What about this then?

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:12.700
That's diagonally across!

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:14.930
So I guess that means that...

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:18.630
What? Don't tell me you thought we have a hamster subscribing?

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:19.380
[HAsu = diagonally, MUkai = across, HAMU = Popular hamster name]

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.910
Of course not!

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:23.590
That's ridiculous.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:27.900
But if it was hamster aliens...

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.690
You're still stuck on that.

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:32.290
We're properly behind schedule.

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:36.190
All right then. The names are all on the right; the symbols and arrows on the left

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:37.900
show the route.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:41.000
What about the places where it says "morn" and "S"?

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.800
"Morn" marks places that only get the morning edition,

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:45.060
and "S" marks places that get the sports section.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.610
The places that have nothing written next to them

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.200
get both the morning and evening editions.

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:56.560
The places marked with "dog" have a dog outside, so be careful there.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:58.150
Y-Yes.

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:01.750
Oh yeah.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.110
Here, take this.

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:08.980
Oh, what a cute puppy!

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:10.210
Look here;

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:13.580
if you pop off the head, it makes an alarm.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.430
Use it if anything ever happens.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:18.120
Oh no, puppy, pull yourself together!

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:18.110
You're not listening...

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:19.780
By tomorrow this needs to be...

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:23.130
Oh look, a convenience store!

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:26.290
There are several along the route, 
so you probably want to take note of them.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:28.780
I see. So we have somewhere to go if we get hungry

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.130
or have to use the bathroom.

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:32.240
Or when someone tries to jump you.

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:36.020
You're joking, right?

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:38.070
Not at all.

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:43.080
Oh god, the puppy, the puppy! He's... He's...!

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:44.930
If you ever get attacked, just yell, "Fire"!

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:47.500
Nobody will come if you just yell, "Help".

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:52.290
Well, how was it?

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:56.200
We basically did a full round.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:58.350
It's dangerous outside, woof.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.560
I'm scared... woof!

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:01.110
What are you talking about?

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:03.560
You want to hear something really scary?

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:06.660
Really... scary?

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.830
A...li...ens...

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:19.860
No, the customers who won't pay for their subscriptions!

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:21.000
It's the customers!

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:25.250
But they're out there, you know:

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:28.140
the people who avoid paying by pretending to be out.

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:34.460
Nothing that a shot from the "Step in Cat Poop Laser" can't fix.

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:36.790
You shouldn't say things like that.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:45.270
Hey?

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:46.190
Yes.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:50.050
Do you want to give it a try this evening?

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:51.780
Can I really?

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:55.440
If you need a bike, we have extras, so just take one of those.

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:57.840
Thank you very much, but...

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:00.700
I don't know how to ride a bike.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.200
Huh?

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:07.650
Did I say something wrong?!

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:22.440
What's going on with everybody?

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:27.000
Maybe they all got brainwashed by aliens!

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:40.360
Hey, pick up the chief and stand up.

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:42.250
Okay.

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:47.650
Is this all right?

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:52.240
That's about how heavy the newspaper load you have to carry is.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:53.690
Really?!

00:08:53.690 --> 00:09:01.040
Which means that every day, we carry home a young girl!

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.960
Hey... Earth to Haru.

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:09.830
Anyway, what that means is that if you can't ride a bike,

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:11.840
there's no way you can make the deliveries.

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:12.860
Got it?

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:13.560
Yes!

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:15.270
I can literally smell the crime.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:20.240
So let's give you your first bike lesson!

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:22.220
Yay!

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:27.010
We can't expect you to be able to ride right off the bat,

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:29.290
so why don't you try first with four wheels?

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:30.060
Okay!

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:32.470
...four wheels!

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:46.560
Jeez!

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:50.780
You really went too far this time Yuuki. I mean, a stroller?!

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:53.730
I was talking about training wheels, what were you thinking?

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:59.650
But Yuuki, there aren't any training wheels for adult bikes.

00:09:59.650 --> 00:10:01.520
I guess you're right.

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:06.840
Want to just use a three-wheeler instead?

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:08.820
A... three wheeler?!

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:18.060
Excuse me, this hurts...

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:20.530
...my special spot.

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:23.930
I see what you're trying to do... the punishment game!

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:28.440
Make her hurt more!

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.440
Will you stop fooling around?

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.760
What are we going to do?

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:40.850
Just kidding!

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:45.950
Noooo!

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:49.150
Kana hates me, chief!

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:53.190
Hey... Earth to Haru.

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:56.840
All right, I'm leaving the rest in your hands.

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:58.020
Okay!

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:02.990
This fight is only just beginning!

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:04.900
What are you talking about?

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:20.940
So how did you all learn how to ride a bike?

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:24.460
Hmm, let me try to remember.

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:26.190
I used training wheels.

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:29.720
What about you, Yume-san?

00:11:30.510 --> 00:11:37.610
The first thing I did was go down a hill THIS STEEP!

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:42.120
And then "Bam!", there was a truck right in front of me!

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:45.200
Yuuki-san!

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:46.670
Oh crap!

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:52.360
It's okay; as you see, I'm still alive!

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:56.090
First someone's gotta do mouth to mouth!

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:57.480
All right!

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:02.040
Uhm... Yuuki-san?

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:05.660
We're going to go do some mouth to mouth now.

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:07.100
For who though?

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:08.180
For me.

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:09.240
But why?

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:11.440
Hurry, so I don't die.

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:18.000
If you have to go to the bathroom during a delivery,

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.820
make sure you go to a convenience store.

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:23.540
All kinds of things go on in the park's bathroom, you see.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.650
Shall we start then?

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:29.160
Teacher, I have a question.

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:31.990
What do you mean by "all kinds of things"?

00:12:34.110 --> 00:12:35.680
Things go on?!

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:43.680
Sorry, occupied.

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:45.590
Jeez!

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:47.130
Excuse me.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:50.730
I guess we have no choice but to start your bike lesson.

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:52.570
Oh, okay!

00:12:58.150 --> 00:13:02.770
This really is the best method to learn how to ride a bike after all!

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:05.430
I see, pushing her back.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:12.860
You're doing great!

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.230
Hang on, Kana!

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:22.790
I'm going to let go soon!

00:13:22.790 --> 00:13:23.820
Don't!

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:25.170
Please don't!

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:27.730
Whatever you do, don't let go!

00:13:29.980 --> 00:13:36.390
Don't let go, don't let go, don't let go, don't let go!

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:38.730
If you let go, it would be so tewwible!

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:44.740
I won't let go!

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:55.710
No! Let go, let go!

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:56.910
Oh you, don't be so coy now.

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:58.330
Method?

00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:00.420
A method that only exists in Haruka's dimension.

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:02.070
Gonna drink 'till I puke!

00:14:02.590 --> 00:14:05.610
All right, I'm going to let go now.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.000
Okay.

00:14:07.850 --> 00:14:08.850
Go!

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:25.400
It's been a while since I saw someone who couldn't pick it up after so many tries.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:31.400
Yeah, but that's what really pushes my buttons.

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:33.860
Are you okay?

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:35.540
Yeah, I'm all right.

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:37.940
Why don't we stop for today?

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:41.650
No please, I'm fine! I can keep going!

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:47.840
But we have to get back soon to get ready for the evening delivery.

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:50.190
Oh...

00:14:55.760 --> 00:15:01.670
Twenty-one, twenty-two, twenty-three, twenty-four...

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:06.260
All right chief, we're off to do the delivery!

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:09.520
It's hot again today, so make sure you keep yourselves hydrated.

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:10.670
Roger!

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:13.310
So, want to race again today, Yuuki?

00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:16.470
The winner gets to lay in the other person's lap
while their ears get cleaned....

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.050
Really?

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:26.110
It's fine. It's not like your life depends on it.

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:32.850
Thank you.

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:36.920
Keep busy.

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:37.710
Yes!

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:41.220
Twenty-three, twenty-four...

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:42.160
You'll never get the delivery done if you space out like that.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.210
But I still can't ride...

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:46.580
What are you talking about?

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:48.360
You can do it on foot.

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:51.690
Right!

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:05.410
Let's see, Mr. Yutakazaki's house is...

00:16:05.870 --> 00:16:07.990
Here it is.

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:12.380
Hey, there's going to be a "Gatsuri Man" special on TV today!

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:14.170
Really? When?!

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:17.500
How should I know? Look in a paper.

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:19.810
What are you talking about?

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:27.000
I guess a newspaper has all kinds of fun and interesting things for people in it.

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:28.480
Congress Totally Confused

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:29.870
Stock Market Crash

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:36.410
I'm sorry, I'm sorry, there's nothing fun in here, I'm sorry!

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:53.780
I'm sure she's fine... right?

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:07.300
I guess I still have ten houses.

00:17:13.610 --> 00:17:15.990
Is someone there?

00:17:22.710 --> 00:17:25.360
Huh? There's no one there.

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:40.540
Maybe it's a gho-ghost...

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:55.660
Oh good, it wasn't a ghost.

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:57.670
How rude!

00:17:57.670 --> 00:18:00.750
How dare you treat me this way?!

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:04.910
Kill yourself in apology, you commoner!

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:05.940
What should I do?

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:08.140
It looks like this girl hit her head hard.

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:10.580
Where's the hospital?

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:13.320
It's the paper with the route!

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:16.440
Don't touch that!

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:18.980
That contains trade secrets!

00:18:18.980 --> 00:18:22.200
So you deliver newspapers too?

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:24.580
How do you know my true form?

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:26.680
You're not a foe to be trifled with...

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:28.930
Well because you have a route book...

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:31.540
Now that it's out...

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:38.750
The rain has stopped.

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:48.600
You're not going to get away with this!

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:49.820
Good day to you!

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:54.940
Huh?

00:18:57.680 --> 00:19:00.280
Is something wrong?

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:08.400
I guess it can't be helped.

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:11.390
If you really want to apologize to me that much,

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:15.260
I suppose I can allow you to escort me to my next delivery.

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:18.220
You're lost, huh?

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:19.610
How rude!

00:19:19.610 --> 00:19:20.740
Let's cut the cheese!

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:21.620
We found it!

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:24.110
Mr. Harimiya with the pine tree on the corner!

00:19:24.110 --> 00:19:30.950
Look, it looks like this address subscribes to both of our papers.

00:19:30.950 --> 00:19:35.590
So if you just follow your route from here, you should get back fine.

00:19:35.590 --> 00:19:39.800
You think I don't know that?

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:44.480
Well, I'll be going then. I still have some work left.

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:46.620
Wait!

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:50.020
What's your name?

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:51.240
I'm Kana.

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:52.840
Kana Nakamachi.

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:03.250
And what's your... huh?

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:16.250
Yeah. Okay. All right.

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:21.160
Haruka says she's almost done and she'll be home soon.

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:22.180
That's good, huh?

00:20:22.180 --> 00:20:24.260
What are you talking about?

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:27.690
I'm only worried about delivery errors and...

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:29.400
I'm sorry!

00:20:33.190 --> 00:20:36.690
Do you have any idea what time it is?

00:20:37.610 --> 00:20:39.210
I'm sorry!

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:42.730
I guess this was a failure:

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:44.780
me delivering newspapers.

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:47.920
The first time I did it, it took me until nine, you know.

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:51.320
I made five wrong deliveries the first time.

00:20:51.320 --> 00:20:54.450
I fell and scattered the delivery all over.

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:57.180
Everyone...

00:20:57.560 --> 00:21:00.640
I guess that was a pass. Barely.

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:03.760
And then you did the right thing, seeking shelter from the rain.

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:04.420
Huh?

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:08.230
It looks like you tried to solve the problem by yourself.

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:10.450
How do you know all about that?

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:11.790
Tada!

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:14.660
This is your day of magnificence!

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:17.120
When did you...?

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:20.240
Shall we eat then?

00:21:20.240 --> 00:21:21.310
All right!

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:24.170
A little...

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:25.800
Don't be like that.

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:28.890
Stop goofing around and get in here already!

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:30.450
That goes for both of you, Haru and Kana!

00:21:31.030 --> 00:21:33.180
What is it?

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:36.020
You called me "Kana".

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:44.730
If you don't hurry up, your food's going to be gone, Kana!

00:21:44.730 --> 00:21:45.900
All right!

00:21:50.220 --> 00:21:55.560
Grandma, today I became Kana, the newspaper delivery girl!

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:58.310
I'm going to have to keep trying hard from today on!

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:35.780
Note: They are playing a Japanese game called Shiritori where you have to say a word that starts with the last syllable of the previous word.

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:35.780
The next episode will be "The First Smile". Ro... Romania.

00:23:35.780 --> 00:23:39.640
A?! Ah... ah... American short hair.

00:23:39.640 --> 00:23:40.730
Antlion larva.

00:23:40.730 --> 00:23:43.820
Mi... Mi... Mika Kujiin...

00:23:43.820 --> 00:23:44.890
Kappa.
